<title>USA: U.S. stockpile sells bauxite to domestic producers.</title>
<headline>U.S. stockpile sells bauxite to domestic producers.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Defense National Stockpile Center sold 300,000 long dry tons of metallurgical grade bauxite, Jamaican type, to Reynolds Metals for $3.135 million on September 27.</p>
<p>The stockpile also sold an additional 300,000 long dry tons of the same grade of bauxite to Kaiser Aluminum for $2.97 million on September 30.</p>
<p>-- New York Commodities 212-859-1646</p>
</text>
